  "insights": [
   "CMS released a proposed rule to tighten oversight of Medicaid supplemental payments, including State Directed Payments (SDPs), by replacing the Average Commercial Rate (ACR) framework with explicit Medicare-based payment caps.",
   "The proposal is estimated to generate $775 billion in total Medicaid savings, including $510 billion in federal savings over 10 years.",
   "Goldman views this as a reinforcement of their existing 'elongated Medicaid underwriting cycle' thesis, suggesting a multi-year margin reset rather than a near-term cyclical trough.",
   "Hospitals (HCA, UHS) are most directly impacted due to high reliance on supplemental payments, while Managed Medicaid MCOs (CNC, MOH, ELV) face second-order risks from potential rate compression and medical cost pressure.",
