 {
  "source": "UBS",
  "title": "The call overwriter\u2019s guide: Identifying stocks for single stock call selling",
  "type": "derivatives",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-05-21",
  "insights": [
   "Selling calls on existing equity positions (covered calls) is an effective way to monetize volatility and generate income, but requires active stock selection to outperform.",
   "Shorter-dated options (e.g., 1-month) generally outperform longer-dated structures because equity markets tend to rise over time, causing longer-dated options to expire in-the-money more frequently.",
   "Defensive option structuring (lower delta, higher strikes) typically delivers a higher frequency of positive returns, even if absolute premium is lower.",
   "The report identifies a 'hype factor' (price-to-sales ratio and net-debt to enterprise value) as a key metric: selling calls on high P/S, low-debt stocks is generally unattractive due to their high-growth, high-volatility nature.",
   "Systematic call overwriting on high-scoring stocks (based on momentum, volatility, and fundamental factors) consistently outperformed long-only portfolios during equity drawdowns.",
   "Option investors trade both underlying price and volatility, making the selection of underlyings for options fundamentally different from selecting stocks for outright long positions."
  ],
  "trades": [
   {
    "description": "Systematic 1-month, 15-delta call overwriting on high-factor-score stocks",
    "rationale": "Captures volatility risk premium and enhances returns during equity drawdowns through active selection.",
    "risk": "Underperformance during strong bull markets due to capped upside; potential for losses if underlying drops significantly.",
    "conviction": "medium",
    "time_horizon": "3-12mo"
   },
   {
    "description": "Long 1-month call options on 'cheap' (low-factor-score) stocks",
    "rationale": "Serves as a portfolio diversifier; performs best when implied volatility underestimates future equity returns.",
    "risk": "Loss of premium paid if the option expires worthless.",
    "conviction": "medium",
    "time_horizon": "1-3mo"
   }
  ],
  "risks": [
   "Capped upside potential in strong upward-trending markets.",
   "Model reliance on historical data which may not persist in future regimes.",
   "Liquidity risk in secondary markets for structured products.",
   "Issuer default risk for reverse convertibles."
  ],
